Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 03:01:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 104/119] docs: the histogram meter, the band, and what it will
 not fix

README gains Auto Darken Time, Metering Mode and the two band percentiles.
ConsoleReference gains r_SceneReferredMeterHistogram, with the reason the
change is a statistic and not a constant - the f * log2(V_hot/V_bg) line that
explains both why the sun never mattered and why the sky always did.
SceneReferredCalibration section 0 is rewritten around the new instrument: how
to read the 64-character bar (a spike hard right is the sun in the saturating
top bin, and the band discarding it is the point), what the band line says, and
that the meter ceiling now belongs to the fallback meter alone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus <noreply@anthropic.com>
