-* **meter ceiling** is where the meter saturates, in pre-exposed units and in stops above mid
-  grey. A texel brighter than this reads as exactly this - an incident meter's dome saturates, and
-  so does this one. It is what stops a sun disc past fp16's range from being read as black; see
-  `scene-notes/decisions/s8-meter-saturation.md`.
+* **meter ceiling** belongs to the fallback meter only and is only printed there. It is where the
+  log-mean meter saturates, in pre-exposed units and in stops above mid grey; a texel brighter
+  than this reads as exactly this, the way an incident meter's dome saturates, which is what stops
+  a sun disc past fp16's range from being read as black
+  (`scene-notes/decisions/s8-meter-saturation.md`). The histogram meter needs no such ceiling: an
+  overflowed texel lands in the top bin, where it has a position and no magnitude, and the
+  percentile band discards it.
 * The Skybox line appends `[no sky texture: term unused]` when the sky material has no diffuse
   texture. In that state the skybox path is not drawn at all and the numbers are informational
   only — this is exactly why the times-ten went unnoticed in stock CRYENGINE.
